msgctxt "#32547"
msgid "When ON, AI translations fetch a human subtitle of the same title in a gender-marking language and use it ONLY to pin down per-line Hebrew gender (he/she, verb/adjective agreement). Tries an out-of-sync Hebrew sub first, then Arabic (marks gender almost 1:1 with Hebrew), then Spanish/French/Russian and more. Falls back silently when nothing aligns. Works for any source language."
msgstr "When ON, AI translations fetch a human subtitle of the same title in a gender-marking language and use it ONLY to pin down per-line Hebrew gender (he/she, verb/adjective agreement). Tries an out-of-sync Hebrew sub first, then Arabic (marks gender almost 1:1 with Hebrew), then Spanish/French/Russian and more. Falls back silently when nothing aligns. Works for any source language."

msgctxt "#32550"
msgid "Fast mode (paid Gemini API tier)"
msgstr "Fast mode (paid Gemini API tier)"

msgctxt "#32551"
msgid "Turn ON only if you are on a PAID Gemini plan (billing enabled on your API key). The add-on normally paces requests and limits parallel chunks to stay under the free tier's ~15 requests/minute limit; a paid key has thousands, so this lifts those limits for much faster translation. Leave OFF for a free key (ON would just cause rate-limit errors and retries). Does not change translation quality -- that is set by the Model option."
msgstr "Turn ON only if you are on a PAID Gemini plan (billing enabled on your API key). The add-on normally paces requests and limits parallel chunks to stay under the free tier's ~15 requests/minute limit; a paid key has thousands, so this lifts those limits for much faster translation. Leave OFF for a free key (ON would just cause rate-limit errors and retries). Does not change translation quality -- that is set by the Model option."

msgctxt "#32556"
msgid "AI translation: gender proofread by a stronger model"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32557"
msgid "When an AI translation finishes (a subtitle picked from the list, or the automatic translation on play), one request to a stronger Gemini model (3.7 Flash, then 3.8, then 3.6 -- about 20 requests a day each on a free key) reads the whole title and corrects the masculine/feminine and singular/plural forms the translator got wrong (who speaks to whom). Only gendered forms change (word endings, את/אתה, הוא/היא...); a correction that touches anything else is dropped. The subtitles show as usual; the corrected file replaces them a few minutes later. When these models are busy or out of quota, the translation stays as it is. A translation made before -- from the cache or the community pool -- is proofread once, the first time it is opened (a pooled one when the subtitle it was translated from is in the list), and the corrected file goes to the pool for everyone. With a paid key this is one more request per title. Measured, of the lines it changed: 3.7 on two films fixed 56 and broke none, 3.8 on one film fixed 34 and broke 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32652"
msgid "Instant subtitles from Ktuvit / Wizdom"
msgstr "Instant subtitles from Ktuvit / Wizdom"

msgctxt "#32653"
msgid "When Ktuvit or Wizdom returns a strong match (90 or more, and at least the minimum below) the subtitle is applied at once, without waiting for the slower sources. The timing is still checked in the background, and one clearly better match can replace it when the full search ends."
msgstr "When Ktuvit or Wizdom returns a strong match (90 or more, and at least the minimum below) the subtitle is applied at once, without waiting for the slower sources. The timing is still checked in the background, and one clearly better match can replace it when the full search ends."

msgctxt "#32654"
